   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Commonwealth Secretariat</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Citizen Political Participation in Governance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Commonwealth has a unique comparative advantage: its trusted convening power, its values-driven Charter, and its direct links with ministries of foreign affairs, justice, youth and gender, media regulators and national human rights institutions across 56 states. It is well-placed to strengthen evidence-based policy, professionalise youth work, and embed inclusion and rights-based approaches in governance systems. By mobilising inter alia youth, women, civil society, and media actors together, the Secretariat can help member states to institutionalise youth and gender mainstreaming, safeguard civic space, and create meaningful opportunities for young people and women to lead and participate in governance at all levels.</narrative>
  </description>
